{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Not by your righteousness and the uprightness of your heart, etc., but by the wickedness of these nations.</b> It would appear that if they had been righteous they would not have been driven out from there — and if so, what would become of the oath to the Fathers? But the matter is thus: the wicked nations deserve to be driven out from there, and even if they had been righteous they would not remain in the land, for the land was a deposit in their hands from the time the Fathers were promised; and the Holy One, blessed be He, could bestow good upon them by giving them another land, for לה' הארץ ומלואה — 'to YHWH is the earth and its fullness.' But this is impossible for them, that they should remain there, in order to fulfill the matter."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:00.690009577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}